  "id": "senegalese_afro_cuban",
  "name": "Senegalese Afro-Cuban dance-band music (Dakar salsa)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Dakar nightclub dance-band music of the 1960s to 1980s in which Senegalese and Gambian bands played Cuban son, pachanga and later salsa learned from imported GV-series 78s, singing in Spanish, Wolof and Mandinka. The bands brought griot vocal styles and Senegalese rhythms into the Cuban forms, preparing the ground for mbalax.",
